' rete — the liveness picture, end to end.
' Every number below is read from source, not remembered:
'   nodus/oevm/zephyr/src/observer.c        WEDGE_SLACK 8, OBSERVER_TICK_MS 1000, OBSERVER_WDT_MS 30000
'   nodus/nsl/lib/kernel.nsl:1807           replyBudget = 2000   (per leg, SPIN-POLLED)
'   nodus/nsl/lib/kernel.nsl:1705,2503      cadMs 30000 / budMs 240000 defaults, ceiling 86400000
'   nodus/oevm/zephyr/PortaBridgeNodeC6.nsl:73,100   cadence 2000, budget = cadence * 8 = 16000
'   porta/internal/space/sweep.go:17        SweepTick = 30 * time.Second
'   porta/internal/space/sweep.go:169..204  verdictFor — the whole decision

@startuml liveness-1-healthy
title One check-in that works — every timeout in play
skinparam backgroundColor #FDFDFD
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 10

box "nodus — one C6" #F2F7FF
  participant "timer ISR\n(Zephyr)" as ISR
  participant "pulse\nmailbox" as MB
  participant "observer thread\n(C)" as OBS
  participant "VM reactor\noevm + PortaBridge" as VM
end box
box "porta — gw85224-01" #FFF6F0
  participant "UDP loop\nwire.Handle" as PW
  participant "store\nexchanges / cells" as ST
  participant "liveness sweep\n(ticker)" as SW
end box

note over ISR, VM #E8F0FE
  **cadMs = 2000** — the base tick, registered by the KERNEL (#231 D1),
  so the deadline exists even for an app that declares no timer.
end note

ISR -> MB : ~#go   //every cadMs//
VM -> MB : pumpEvents  //(K_FOREVER)//
MB -> VM : ~#go        <b>pulse_drained()++</b>

activate VM
VM -> PW : **pull** { nodeId, bootId, cursor }\n//~40 B — one 6LoWPAN fragment//
activate VM #FFD98A
note right of VM #FFD98A
  <b>awaitReply: replyBudget = 2000 ms</b>
  A SPIN, not a block: it polls
  `socket receive` until the deadline.
end note
PW -> ST : stamp exchanges(ts_ms, **boot_id**)
note right of ST : one row per REQUEST — and **both** legs\nstamp nodes.last_seen_ms via RecordExchange.\nNo `leg` column since #231 D4 deleted its only reader.
PW --> VM : **#batch**  //<= 512 B//
deactivate VM

VM -> VM : applyBatch → publishApps →\napplyLivenessGoal → publishLiveness →\npublishMetrics → publishCheap
VM -> PW : **push** { entries }\n//<= 512 B — 5-6 fragments, all must survive//
activate VM #FFD98A
note right of VM #FFD98A : <b>awaitReply: 2000 ms again</b>\nSecond leg, second budget.
PW --> VM : **#ack**
deactivate VM
deactivate VM

== meanwhile, on its own thread ==
OBS -> MB : //every **1000 ms**//: pulse_pending(), pulse_drained()
note right of OBS #E6F4EA
  <b>wedge deadline = shortest declared period x WEDGE_SLACK(8) = 16000 ms</b>
  Since rete#269 it fires on **frozen progress**, not on mailbox depth.
  Backstop for this thread dying: task_wdt 30000 ms → hw reset.
end note

== and, on porta's own clock ==
SW -> ST : //every **SweepTick = 30000 ms**//\n`now - last_seen > bud` ?
note right of SW #E6F4EA
  bud is the number the **NODE** declared (#231 D4).
  Bench node: cadence 2000, budget cadence x 8 = **16000**.
  Order: neverSeen → no-budget:unknown → live → deaf:unknown → silent.
end note
@enduml


@startuml liveness-2-silent
title The same node with its uplink gone — where the numbers stop agreeing
skinparam backgroundColor #FDFDFD
skinparam ParticipantPadding 8
skinparam BoxPadding 10

box "nodus — one C6" #F2F7FF
  participant "pulse\nmailbox" as MB
  participant "observer thread\n(C, 1000 ms)" as OBS
  participant "VM reactor" as VM
end box
box "porta" #FFF6F0
  participant "UDP loop" as PW
  participant "store" as ST
  participant "liveness sweep" as SW
end box

MB -> VM : ~#go  //(cad 2000)//
activate VM
VM -> PW : pull
activate VM #FFB3B3
VM -> VM : ...spins the full **2000 ms**...
note right of VM #FFB3B3 : nothing arrives → **misses++**
deactivate VM
VM -> PW : push
activate VM #FFB3B3
VM -> VM : ...spins the full **2000 ms**...
note right of VM #FFB3B3 : nothing arrives → **misses++**
deactivate VM
deactivate VM

note over MB, VM #FFF3CD
  <b>The tick now costs ~4.007 s against a DECLARED cadence of 2000 ms.</b>
  Measured on c6spare 2026-08-27. Nothing anywhere re-derives from the
  delivered period — every deadline downstream still comes from the 2000.
end note

OBS -> MB : sample #1 .. #16 (1001 ms apart)
note right of OBS #FFB3B3
  <b>rete#269, now fixed:</b> this used to judge mailbox DEPTH at
  an instant. 4 samples span 4004 ms against a 4007 ms cycle, so a
  3 ms beat walked the one sample that saw the empty window out of it,
  and the detector rebooted a HEALTHY node at exactly 8 x cad.
  Judging `pulse_drained()` — progress — cannot alias.
end note

... the node keeps ticking, `misses` climbs 2 per tick ...

SW -> ST : now - last_seen > bud(16000) ?
ST --> SW : yes → **#silent**
note right of SW #FFF3CD
  But only at the NEXT 30 s sweep. The node declared 16 s;
  porta cannot form a verdict faster than 30 s.
end note
@enduml


