@startuml liveness-4-holes
title Where the holes are — liveness, both halves
skinparam backgroundColor #FDFDFD
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam ArrowColor #444
left to right direction

package "nodus — the node" #F2F7FF {
  component "kernel base tick\n**cad** declared by the app\n(kernel.nsl:2579)" as CAD
  component "checkIn: pull then push\n**awaitReply spins 2000 ms per leg**\n(kernel.nsl:1807, 2845)" as CHK
  component "misses counter\npublished in sys/metrics\n(kernel.nsl:2333)" as MIS
  component "observer thread, C\nsamples 1000 ms\ndeadline = shortest x **8**\n(observer.c:67,159)" as OBS
}

package "porta — the gateway" #FFF6F0 {
  component "exchanges row per check-in\nts_ms + **boot_id**\n(schema.go:118)" as EXC
  component "liveness sweep\n**SweepTick = 30 s**\n(sweep.go:17)" as SWP
  component "verdictFor\nnow - last_seen > **bud**\n(sweep.go:169)" as VER
}

CAD --> CHK
CHK --> EXC : pull / push  (UDP+CBOR)
CHK --> MIS
EXC --> SWP
SWP --> VER

note bottom of CHK #FFD5D5
  <b>H1 — the declared cadence is a promise nothing checks.</b>
  Delivered period = cad + 2 x replyBudget. At cad 2000 under a
  silent uplink that is 4.007 s, twice the declaration. Every
  deadline downstream still derives from the declared 2 s.
  This is what rete#269 aliased on; the fix made the DETECTOR
  immune, not the MODEL.
end note

note bottom of MIS #FFD5D5
  <b>H5 — misses is unreportable exactly when it matters.</b>
  It rides sys/metrics on the PUSH leg — the leg that is failing.
  2026-08-27: misses reached 1281 and porta learned nothing.

  <b>H7 — the node never acts on its own silence.</b>
  No backoff, no escalation, no local reboot after N misses.
  The only actor that can decide is the one it cannot reach.
end note

note bottom of OBS #FFD5D5
  <b>H4 — two independent eights that happen to agree.</b>
  WEDGE_SLACK=8 in C; the published budget is cadence x 8 in nsl.
  CLAIMS.md: "neither derives from the other". Both read 16000
  today — move one and they diverge in silence.

  <b>H6 — no timer, no judgement.</b>
  observer_verdict returns COND_NONE when zero timers are declared.
  The kernel base tick closes that — but startTicking: sits
  downstream of the socket bind, so a boot whose bind fails has
  no timer, no deadline, and no detector.
end note

note bottom of SWP #FFD5D5
  <b>H2 — porta cannot honour a budget shorter than its own sweep.</b>
  SweepTick 30 s vs the bench node's declared bud 16 s. #231 D4 says
  "porta infers nothing" — but detection latency is capped by a
  porta-side constant for every node on this bench. Worst case
  bud + 30 s = 46 s.
end note

note bottom of VER #FFD5D5
  <b>H3 — the verdict cannot see a reboot loop.</b>
  verdictFor consults last_seen and bud only — ARRIVAL TIMES, never
  boot_id, which is NOT NULL on every exchanges row. A node that
  wedges, reboots and speaks again forever reads #live for as long as
  its loop period stays under bud: PERMANENTLY at the kernel default
  (bud 240 s, kernel.nsl:1705), and intermittently at the bench node's
  16 s, where the verdict flickers on the beat between the ~21 s
  silence gap and the 30 s sweep rather than on the node's health.
  One join on boot_id would settle it.

  <b>H8 — porta's deafness is modelled, the node's is not.</b>
  WasDeaf yields #unknown when PORTA was not listening. There is no
  mirror: a node wedged for most of the window still reads #live off
  one late check-in, because speech outranks everything.
end note
@enduml
